  "details": "The string 130880 is troublesome in French for multiple reasons:\n\nFirst: The variables for the keybinds are broken in French, as seen in the screens.\n\nSecond: Some key words are untranslated and not found on Crowdin, \"Content\" and \"Portal\".\n\nThird: I would like the string to be split in three for each type: \"Portal\", \"Content\" and \"Sticker\" as it is impossible in French to correctly write them.\n\nFor example, in French, the correct way for each type would be \"Appuyez sur {0} pour placer le contenu [....]\" ; \"Appuyez sur {0} pour placer le portail [...]\" ; \"Appuyez sur {0} pour placer l'autocollant [...]\".\n\nThere is actually old strings that were used for the \"Portal\"  and \"Sticker\". For some reasons however, they were deprecated and a single string is now in use with \"Portal\", \"Sticker\" and \"Content\" locked behind a variable.",
